[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. It holds more than one bug.
The desk merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every
report about a date has a subject that looks like every other. Read by tenant, channel and body,
the reports split three ways.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 fixes the shared parser only. The other two problems keep coming in
after it ships, and each now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## How each report was placed

1. **`hint`**: the report came in through the booking form, and the tenant runs `booking-v3`.
   That form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date, so day-first people type the month first, and the
   form then reads it day first. The parser fix does not touch this: the hint has to change.
2. **`one-day`**: the desk read the body as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). Day and month are
   right; the date is a day early or late, and in one report differs between Lisbon and Toronto.
   A swap can't do that. It is a time-zone or date-boundary bug.
3. **`parser`**: everything else from a day-first tenant. The shared parser reads the date month
   first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 describes.

Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, so it isn't used here. The tenant directory
decides.

## What the old page showed

The table on the #4471 page, for comparison. It finds `hint` but files the one-day moves under
`parser`, footnoted, and leaves `hint` without a ticket.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Before you merge a report into a big ticket, check it has the same cause, not the same subject.
- A one-day move isn't a swap. Don't merge it into #4471.
- New `booking-v3` form reports from day-first tenants go to the `hint` ticket.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
